<title>USA: U.S. cash soymeal - Basis offers mostly unchanged.</title>
<headline>U.S. cash soymeal - Basis offers mostly unchanged.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-04-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Most soymeal basis offers were unchanged Wednesday despite a recent reduction in production of U.S. soymeal, dealers said.</p>
<p>&quot;We dropped the crush by three million bushels last week, and the basis is not doing what we thought it would,&quot; said an Indiana dealer. &quot;The pipeline must be pretty full.&quot;</p>
<p>Brokers said both domestic and export demand for soymeal remained soft, and there was only light trade in cash markets early Wednesday.</p>
<p>&quot;It's still really quiet on the river and there's not much trading today (Wednesday) at all,&quot; said one river dealer.</p>
<p>Because cash soybean basis has been moving higher, soymeal basis will also have to climb or crushers might be forced to take unscheduled downtime, one dealer said..</p>
